data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":741,"item_id":"fc_04de6b92baab60ea016adb45d97b208191a89638fb6c95fcab","output_index":1,"arguments":"{\"artifact_json\":\"{\\\"base_candidate\\\":27,\\\"patches\\\":[{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/4/locals\\\",\\\"value\\\":[{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"r\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"positive real\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"R004\\\",\\\"start\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"end\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"arbitrary\\\",\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"Fix arbitrary r>0.\\\",\\\"from_inputs\\\":[],\\\"from_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[]},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"j\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"Fin n spatial coordinate index\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"R004\\\",\\\"start\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"end\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"arbitrary\\\",\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"Fix an arbitrary spatial coordinate index j∈Fin n for the integration-by-parts calculation; the resulting identity is then summed over all j.\\\",\\\"from_inputs\\\":[],\\\"from_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"n\\\"]},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"v_j\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"the jth standard basis vector of ℝⁿ\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"R004\\\",\\\"start\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"end\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"definition\\\",\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"Let v_j be the jth standard basis vector in ℝⁿ.\\\",\\\"from_inputs\\\":[],\\\"from_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"j\\\",\\\"n\\\"]},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"f_j\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"ℝⁿ→ℝᵐ\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"R004\\\",\\\"start\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"end\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"definition\\\",\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"Define f_j(x)=∂_{x_j}u(x,r).\\\",\\\"from_inputs\\\":[],\\\"from_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"u\\\",\\\"j\\\",\\\"r\\\"]},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"g\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"ℝⁿ→ℝᵐ\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"R004\\\",\\\"start\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"end\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"definition\\\",\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"Define g(x)=u_t(x,r).\\\",\\\"from_inputs\\\":[],\\\"from_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"u\\\",\\\"r\\\"]}]},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/4/argument/0/text\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"Fix arbitrary r>0 and spatial index j∈Fin n; define v_j=e_j, f_j(x)=∂_{x_j}u(x,r), and g(x)=u_t(x,r). N001 directly supplies a closed time window containing r and a compact C outside which u=q throughout that window. Because u is jointly smooth and is constant on the open set (ℝⁿ\\\\\\\\C)×J, f_j,g and their Frechet derivatives vanish outside C and are continuous. Thus the three functions ⟨Df_j(x)[v_j],g(x)⟩, ⟨f_j(x),Dg(x)[v_j]⟩, and ⟨f_j(x),g(x)⟩ are continuous and supported in C. By M001, once the ambient finite-on-compacts property proved in R002 is instantiated, all three are integrable. Smoothness gives the Frechet derivative identities everywhere, in particular on tsupport(g) for f_j and tsupport(f_j) for g. Apply M011 with X=ℝⁿ, F=G=ℝᵐ, W=ℝ, B the Euclidean dot product and direction v_j. It gives ∫⟨∂_{x_j}u,∂_{x_j}u_t⟩=−∫⟨∂_{x_jx_j}u,u_t⟩. Since j was arbitrary, sum these identities over j=1,…,n. The finite-dimensional product rule yields ∫e_t=2∫u_t·(u_{tt}−Δ_xu). N002 identifies E′(r)=∫e_t, proving N003 for arbitrary r>0.\\\"}]}\"}"}

